# GI-TWOSIDED-BIAS: a traced hit on a mostly two-sided mesh (foliage) reads the surface cache with its bias grown by
# 50 cm, as UE SampleLumenMeshCards (bMostlyTwoSided). Thin leaves are captured from both faces, so a hit on either
# face lies far from the depth one card captured; without the extra bias the hit fell through to "back face"/uncovered
# and the crown shaded itself dark in the GI. GI is forced to SoftwareTraced (the Mac tracer), not the PPV's request.
# The before frame (1_before) is the same scenario run on origin/dev's shaders; this file names the after frames.
Проект ../BistroFoliageProj/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/B16_Bistro_Street.desce
Дано run Quality "Quality: GlobalIllumination.Method SoftwareTraced"
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position -440,300,-230
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction -0.6,0.05,-0.8
Тогда-вид 2_after плющ и кусты в GI без тёмных пятен внутри листвы, которых нет в 3_gioff (в 1_before они есть)
Когда run View "View mode: Indirect Lighting (GI)"
Тогда-вид 2b_after_indirect непрямой свет листвы ровный, без чёрных провалов внутри кроны
Когда run View "View mode: Lit"
Когда run Quality "Quality: GlobalIllumination.Method Off"
Тогда-вид 3_gioff та же листва без GI: эталон, где самозатенения нет
Когда run Quality "Quality: GlobalIllumination.Method Level"
